{
  "estimator": "Aalen-Johansen nonparametric cumulative incidence function for ED return, with death within 30 days of index discharge treated as a competing event; patients without either event censored at 30 days",
  "population": "MIMIC-IV-ED, treated adult headache index visits discharged home",
  "n_discharged": 8346,
  "horizon_days": 30.0,
  "grid_step_days": 0.25,
  "n_return": 999,
  "n_death_without_return": 3,
  "n_death_after_return": 2,
  "death_times_recovered": true,
  "death_time_source": "MIMIC-IV hosp/patients.csv.gz dod, re-merged on subject_id; t_death = dod - index outtime. Reproduces the parquet's died_30d flag for all cohort rows. dod is date-granular (all timestamps midnight), so deaths are resolved to the day.",
  "n_censored_before_30d": null,
  "censoring_note": "Not determinable as a count. MIMIC-IV shifts every patient's dates by a random per-patient offset (cohort index intime spans 2110 to 2210 for care delivered in the 2010s), so end-of-window truncation cannot be identified by calendar date across patients. Two shift-invariant checks were combined instead. 8165 of 8346 discharged patients (97.8%) have demonstrably complete 30-day follow-up, either because their own record (ED, hospital, or death) extends at least 30 days past the index discharge or because the interval from their anchor year to the end of ED data collection guarantees it under the worst-case assumption about their true anchor year. For the remaining 181 (2.2%) the data cannot establish whether follow-up was truncated, so no censoring count is reported. The primary estimate censors all patients at 30 days; worst_case_admin_censoring censors these patients at their verified window instead and is reported as a bound.",
  "followup_verification": {
    "n_discharged": 8346,
    "n_verified_30d_followup": 8165,
    "n_indeterminate": 181,
    "pct_verified": 97.83,
    "collection_end_estimates_by_anchor_group": {
      "2008 - 2010": 2020.868,
      "2011 - 2013": 2020.919,
      "2014 - 2016": 2020.838,
      "2017 - 2019": 2020.901
    },
    "collection_end_used": 2020.838,
    "method": "verified if max(own last ED/hospital/death record - index outtime, guaranteed window from anchor_year to the calibrated end of ED data collection under the worst-case anchor year) >= 30 days"
  },
  "return_time_defect": {
    "status": "Repaired at source. Counts below are the residual contamination in the parquet as read by this run and must be zero.",
    "n_rows_cohort": 0,
    "n_rows_discharged": 0,
    "cause": "02_cohort.py originally collapsed to the index visit with groupby('subject_id').first(), which returns the first NON-NULL value per column. t_ret_d is null whenever the index visit had no 30-day return, so 193 cohort rows (151 discharged) inherited a later visit's return time and added spurious early returns to the cumulative-incidence curve. Boolean outcomes could not be affected; gap_h, ret_72h, ret_7d and ret_30d were each re-derived from edstays and reproduce exactly, and the headline estimates were unchanged by the repair.",
    "remedy": "02_cohort.py now collapses with groupby('subject_id').nth(0), a true first-row selection, so the parquet stores each patient's own index-visit return time. This script re-derives the return time from the independently verified gap_h and checks it against the stored column in both directions; the counts above are that check."
  },
  "max_abs_diff_vs_naive_pp": 0.0,
  "max_abs_diff_vs_naive_corrected_pp": 0.0,
  "max_abs_diff_worst_case_censoring_pp": 0.238,
  "n_worst_case_censored_before_30d": 170,
  "estimator_identity_note": "With no censoring before the horizon the number at risk at time t is n minus the events already observed, so S(t-) = Y(t)/n and the Aalen-Johansen increment reduces to d1(t)/n. Under the primary censoring assumption the estimator is therefore algebraically identical to the cumulative proportion of returns, which is why both max_abs_diff_vs_naive_corrected_pp and max_abs_diff_vs_naive_pp are zero. The first compares the estimator against a cumulative proportion rebuilt here from the verified gap_h; the second compares it against a cumulative proportion computed from t_ret_d as the parquet stores it, and is zero only because the inherited-return-time defect has been repaired at source. Naming the estimator does not move the curve.",
